WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
Pulling up to another day of Tesla's short time,

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.480
daily, episode 486, coming to you from Vancouver,

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.320
it's May 27th, 2026.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.440
Tesla never sleeps and neither does the new cycle.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.960
Tesla's dry cathode process could slash battery production costs

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.200
as Elon confirms the text potential.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.600
Elon Musk stated that the dry cathode manufacturing method

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.740
under development at Tesla could cut battery costs

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.000
in a meaningful way.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.040
The approach eliminates solvents during electrode production,

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.540
which simplifies the process and reduces equipment needs.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.360
This change targets one of the largest remaining cost drivers

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.620
in cell manufacturing.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.440
The update comes as Tesla continues

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.680
scaling 4680 cell output at Giga, Texas.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.540
Next data point to watch is any update

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.400
on pilot line yields during the upcoming earnings call.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.200
Taking a step back from today's headlines,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.620
the confirmation that dry cathode electrode production

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.880
could meaningfully lower cell costs

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.940
challenges the assumption that incremental chemistry tweaks

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.640
are the only remaining levers for battery economics.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.820
The process removes solvents and associated drying ovens

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.160
from the manufacturing line,

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.100
which historically account for a sizable share

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.400
of capital and energy expenditure per kilowatt hour.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.740
Real-world pilot data from other manufacturers

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.620
has shown solvent-free lines cutting those costs

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:27.860
by roughly 20 to 30% once yield stabilized.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.380
Though Tesla has not yet published its own internal figures.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.700
If the approach scales inside Tesla's vertically

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:35.980
integrated cell production,

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.720
it would reduce reliance on external suppliers

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.560
for both equipment and materials

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.920
while tightening the link between cell cost and pack price,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.680
potentially widening the gap between Tesla

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.300
and competitors still dependent

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.120
on conventional wet processes.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.420
Now shifting focus to how software changes

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.840
are altering daily driving.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.280
Owners testing version 14.3.3 report fewer interventions

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.220
from the driver monitoring system during routine drives.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.060
The update reduces chime frequency

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.940
when adjusting music or navigation,

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.600
allowing brief glances away from the road

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.860
without immediate alerts.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.940
Testors note the change makes the system feel less intrusive

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.020
on familiar roots.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.940
The improvement stems from refined attention

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.920
monitoring thresholds and the latest software branch.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.160
Watch for broader rollout metrics in the coming weeks.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.860
That software refinement pairs with ongoing sales strength

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:30.920
for the Model Y.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.720
Elon Musk reiterated that strong product execution

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.400
outweighs brand perception and driving sales.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:41.780
He pointed to the Model Y continuing to lead EV registrations

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.080
even amid ongoing public discussion around the company.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.900
The comment underscores Tesla's focus

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.160
on simplifying the ownership experience

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.840
rather than marketing campaigns.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.500
Recent European registration data shows the model maintaining

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.300
its position at the top of the segment.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.520
Next indicator will be may delivery figures.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.160
Strong volume in Europe raises questions

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.820
about supporting infrastructure for higher power needs.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.080
Reports indicate Texas sites are under consideration

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.360
for the initial deployment of Tesla's

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.580
one megawatts megacharger network.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.160
The charger's target commercial fleets

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.920
and upcoming vehicle platforms requiring higher power delivery.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.120
Location selection focuses on corridors

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.440
with existing high voltage infrastructure.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.500
This rollout would mark the first public use

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.920
of the new hardware outside test facilities.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.660
Fleet operators will be watching for permitting timelines.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.260
As hardware expands, real-world battery data

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:40.380
offers separate reassurance on longevity.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.460
Independent testing of a 2017 Model S

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.020
showed the battery retaining usable capacity

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.740
after nine years of service.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.940
The avalued diagnostic measured degradation

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.340
under controlled conditions

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.920
rather than relying on dashboard estimates.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.340
Results provide one of the longer

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.200
real-world data points for early Tesla packs.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.160
The test highlights how thermal management

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.160
and charge habits influence longevity.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.140
Future reports on similar vintage vehicles

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.100
will add context.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.220
Battery longevity data intersects with current market trends

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.160
for used vehicles.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.620
Recent market data shows Tesla resale prices

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.340
fell 5.3% over the past year

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.100
while other segments recovered.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.520
The trend affects multiple model years and trims.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.320
Owners and buyers are watching

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.900
whether new inventory pricing or software updates

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:31.900
alter the trajectory.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.140
High production volumes and frequent updates

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.360
continue to weigh on residual values.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.280
The company has not announced specific programs

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.220
to support used market stability.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.780
Resale softness partly reflects a maturing fleet

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.520
which is also creating new service opportunities.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.540
Independent shops are adapting service bays

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.120
and training programs to handle high-voltage systems

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.820
and software diagnostics.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.500
The shift reflects growing fleet age

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.720
and demand for non-dealer options.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.760
Tesla's direct sales model has left gaps

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.820
that specialized third-party facilities are now failing.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.740
Technicians cite the need for updated certification programs

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.060
focused on battery and inverter work.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:14.820
Expansion of these shops

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.940
will depend on parts availability and training throughput.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.320
While the existing lineup ages and needs service

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.500
older halo models may not be finished yet.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.520
A Tesla Vice President indicated the company

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.400
has not ruled out future updates to the Model S

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.760
and Model X lines.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.500
The comments leave open the possibility

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.260
of refreshed versions even as production focus

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.040
remains on newer platforms.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.980
Current output continues at low volumes

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.940
while the company evaluates demand.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.800
The statement contrasts with earlier signals

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.800
that the models were being phased down.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.580
Any concrete plans would likely surface

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.740
in product announcements later this year.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.900
Hardware questions aside,

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.280
Tesla is also patenting solutions for vision challenges

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.820
that affect both vehicles and robots.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.760
Tesla received a patent for a lens cleaning system

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.980
designed to maintain camera clarity

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.680
without large external washer nozzles.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.540
The mechanism targets debris buildup

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.920
that affects both vehicle autonomy sensors

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.620
and optimist robot vision.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.500
The design integrates a wiper directly into the housing

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.600
to reduce fluid use and complexity.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.780
This addresses a known limitation in vision

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:30.020
only systems operating in dirty or wet conditions.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.020
Deployment timing on production hardware

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.200
remains to be seen.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.520
Keep an eye on may delivery figures

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.820
and any earnings call updates on 4680 yields.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:41.980
That's your Tesla news for today.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.260
TSLA closed at $433.59,

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.880
up $7.58, 1.8%.

